{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1506108-i-have-exalted-2nd-edition-how-different-is-3rd-edition","id":1506108,"title":"I have Exalted 2nd edition - how different is 3rd edition?","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Exalted"],"posts":[{"date":"2023-03-21T19:28:38-07:00","id":1506108,"title":"I have Exalted 2nd edition - how different is 3rd edition?","content":"So I have new books of 2nd edition exalted: Rules, Screen, Storytellers Companion, and the Scavenger Sons Sourcebook. How different is 3rd edition and are these books still useful? Thanks!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27867-brasidas19004","name":"brasidas19004","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2023"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-03-21T21:22:48-07:00","id":1506115,"title":"","content":"Unfortunately their use will be extremely limited for running third edition, except perhaps as finding kernels of plot inspiration. Pretty much all of the basic mechanical systems beyond &quot;roll attribute + ability vs a difficulty&quot; have dramatically changed, and the setting has undergone significant changes from 2e as well - things are more left to mystery rather than overexamined as in 2e, the non-Solar Exalted have actual places in the setting other than &quot;inept babies sitting around as the world dies around them because only the Solars can do anything&quot;...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1},{"type":"\ud83d\udc4e","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/756-meianno-yuurei","name":"Meianno Yuurei","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar756_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"541"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-03-21T21:25:48-07:00","id":1506116,"title":"","content":"Creatures are still good to use on the behavior and types category, but mechanically yeah not so much,.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3400-nalak42","name":"nalak42","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3400_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2931"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-03-22T01:12:23-07:00","id":1506126,"title":"","content":"Scavenger Sons is from 1st edition, and in my opinion is probably still the best setting book to use for 3rd edition until the new Across the 8 Directions book comes out for 3E. Highly recommend using it for 3E in the meantime.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26886-lindharin","name":"Lindharin","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"33"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-03-22T02:55:44-07:00","id":1506130,"title":"","content":"Scavenger Sons, as a setting book, is still highly useful in giving a slightly more detailed view of specific chunks of the setting than any of the core books will give.<br /> <br /> Storyteller Companion does have some setting discussion regarding non-Solar Exalt types and spirits, but the mechanics aren't going to be much use.<br /> <br /> The 2E core has slightly more word count on most of the setting locations it covers, but it's going to be mostly the same information as the 3E core, just less compressed as each edition has added slightly more to the core setting.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":2433,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2433-highpriest","user":"HighPriest","date":". 03-22-2023, 07:02 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2433-highpriest","name":"HighPriest","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2433_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"360"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-03-22T12:13:39-07:00","id":1506159,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>HighPriest</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1506108-i-have-exalted-2nd-edition-how-different-is-3rd-edition?p=1506130#post1506130\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Scavenger Sons, as a setting book, is still highly useful in giving a slightly more detailed view of specific chunks of the setting than any of the core books will give.<br /> <br /> Storyteller Companion does have some setting discussion regarding non-Solar Exalt types and spirits, but the mechanics aren't going to be much use.<br /> <br /> The 2E core has slightly more word count on most of the setting locations it covers, but it's going to be mostly the same information as the 3E core, just less compressed as each edition has added slightly more to the core setting.</div> </div> </div> </div>All, thanks for replies! Are some people still playing 2ed? Is it like D&amp;D where there are many versions being played at any given time? If so, how would I find 2ed. people? Thanks!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27867-brasidas19004","name":"brasidas19004","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2023"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-03-22T13:36:03-07:00","id":1506170,"title":"","content":"<i>Scavenger Sons</i> is a 1e book, actually. So even some of how it presents things in the 2e corebook, its sourcebooks, and how 3e presents some things do differ. Thre is an upcoming book, <i>Across the 8 Directions</i>, which is around twice the size but similar format of an atlas of the setting coming out sometime in the next year or so for 3e. And various lcoations on it get retreaded a bit in different forms in both editions.<br /> <br /> The 2e corebook is good for 2e, and such, but will generlaly not be as well-known to folks these days. And while it has some of the broad-strokes similarities to the 1e and 3e books, each edition of Exalted is a soft reboot of the setting, and so will often reuslt in some things being broadly similar, and other things in the specifics being notably different. An analogy i tend to use is say, Batman or Spider-Man movies, where some things are broadly the same like the charact,er their aesthetic, their abilities, or their main city, but a lot of details vary between different film versions, animated interpreations, or video games.<br /> <br /> The Storyteller's Companion books for 1e and 2e ultimatley are kind of &quot;spillover&quot; books, containing things like NPC rules and Charms, some misc. artifacts, and subsystems that couldn't make it into the corebook of that edition. In gneeral the information in them gets supplanted by later books in their editions.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>And stuff.<br /> <sub><a href=\"https://blaqueandstuff.deviantart.com/\" target=\"_blank\">My DeviantArt Page</a> // <a href=\"http://blaqueandstuff.tumblr.com/\" target=\"_blank\">My tumblr</a> // <a href=\"http://www.dropbox.com/sh/trxegr5hl27s1l5/AAAegBBzxbDhvk1YpYJqdhz8a?dl=0\" target=\"_blank\">Exalted 3e Houserules</a></sub>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/353-blaque","name":"Blaque","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar353_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2976"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-03-22T13:39:43-07:00","id":1506171,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>brasidas19004</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1506108-i-have-exalted-2nd-edition-how-different-is-3rd-edition?p=1506159#post1506159\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> All, thanks for replies! Are some people still playing 2ed? Is it like D&amp;D where there are many versions being played at any given time? If so, how would I find 2ed. people? Thanks!</div> </div> </div> </div>I think a lot of games are mostly 3e these days as that is the most readily accessable edition. This is especailly now with the soon final relase of <i>Exalted Essence</i>, whcih is kind of an abridged version of the 3e rules which includes all canon Exalts for 3e as playable. The main fancord and here are obviously pretty 3e focused, as are forums like Sword of Creation. My main thing to keep in mind is that if you do explore 2e games, like with any game, there is probably a factor of folks being ovelry hostile to other editions or changes to the setting between them (see my prior post about different Spider-Man movies.)<br /> <br /> A really good take on the differences between editions and what is important to highlgiht of those differences can be found with this for-free thing from OPP itself and its fan content writing guideleins. This helps in showcasing where to go depending on which edition seesm more appealing I think.<br /> <div class=\"b-bbcode b-bbcode__url b-bbcode__url--preview\"> <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/252122/Exalted-Storytellers-Vault-Style-Guide\" target=\"_blank\" class=\"urlimg_container\"> <img class=\"js-img-fallback\" src=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/images/1/252122.jpg\"> </a> <div class=\"urlinfo\"> <div class=\"title ellipsis\"> <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/252122/Exalted-Storytellers-Vault-Style-Guide\" target=\"_blank\"> Exalted Storytellers Vault Style Guide - White Wolf | Storytellers Vault </a> </div> <div class=\"url ellipsis\"> <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/252122/Exalted-Storytellers-Vault-Style-Guide\" target=\"_blank\"> https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/252122/Exalted-Storytellers-Vault-Style-Guide </a> </div> <div class=\"meta\"> Exalted Storytellers Vault Style Guide - Welcome to the Exalted Storytellers Vault Style Guide. This guide exists to help you create new material for any edition </div> </div> </div>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>And stuff.<br /> <sub><a href=\"https://blaqueandstuff.deviantart.com/\" target=\"_blank\">My DeviantArt Page</a> // <a href=\"http://blaqueandstuff.tumblr.com/\" target=\"_blank\">My tumblr</a> // <a href=\"http://www.dropbox.com/sh/trxegr5hl27s1l5/AAAegBBzxbDhvk1YpYJqdhz8a?dl=0\" target=\"_blank\">Exalted 3e Houserules</a></sub>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/353-blaque","name":"Blaque","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar353_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2976"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-06-03T07:58:11-07:00","id":1513771,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>brasidas19004</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1506108-i-have-exalted-2nd-edition-how-different-is-3rd-edition?p=1506159#post1506159\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> All, thanks for replies! Are some people still playing 2ed? Is it like D&amp;D where there are many versions being played at any given time? If so, how would I find 2ed. people? Thanks!</div> </div> </div> </div>Yes.<br /> <br /> Just that I think most of us have pretty much given up with forums where 2e posts are supposed to go to the same section as Ex3 stuff (unless it is for all RPGs, but in the same vein I don't bother to post about other RPGs where it has to share the same posting space as D&amp;D).<br /> <br /> There's a Discord server named Exalted RPG that has a 2e channel for talking about 2e stuff. While not as active as the channels for 3e stuff, it is far from dead.<br /> <br /> Personally, I don't have an active Exalted game at the moment, as I will work 80% and study 50% for the next two years, so I don't have time for it. However, when I do run a game it is mainly 2.5. Maybe 50% is 2/2.5, and the other 50% is from 1st and 3rd edition, and my own stuff.<br /> <br /> From 3rd edition, I have mainly pilfered the map (but I don't use the writeup for the new sea in the SE corner) and the new intimacy and social combat system. As I'm not that much of a rules-as-written ST/GM, I haven't really bothered to integrate the mechanics for it into 2e.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2839-lundgren","name":"Lundgren","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"523"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-10-16T19:38:03-07:00","id":1524172,"title":"","content":"If you're going to run 2e, the best thing to pilfer from 3e are the Sorcerous Workings. Simply excellent, IMO.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2783-tytalus","name":"Tytalus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2783_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"491"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}